1
00:00:06,050 --> 00:00:10,330
OK, Philip. This is your third cup of coffee.

2
00:00:10,330 --> 00:00:11,590
We should get to work,

3
00:00:11,590 --> 00:00:14,780
or we won't be finished by dinnertime.

4
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:16,360
I guess we must.

5
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:19,370
We must.

6
00:00:19,370 --> 00:00:31,170
OK. The beginning of my famous Thanksgiving apple pie.

7
00:00:31,170 --> 00:00:37,650
One apple. Two apples. Three apples. Four apples.

8
00:00:37,650 --> 00:00:39,370
Come on, Philip!

9
00:00:39,370 --> 00:00:41,580
Get busy with your famous apple pie.

10
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:43,410
There's much more to be done.

11
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:44,440
Now, the ingredients.

12
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:45,890
What goes into my apple pie besides apples?

13
00:00:45,890 --> 00:01:02,320
Ah, yes. Flour, sugar, butter.

14
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:06,150
Butter, nice and cold and hard.

15
00:01:06,150 --> 00:01:08,410
OK, here are the walnuts.

16
00:01:08,410 --> 00:01:09,920
Last but not least,

17
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:15,100
the reason my apple pie is famous--cinnamon.

18
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:18,830
Cinnamon ...

19
00:01:18,830 --> 00:01:20,710
Ellen, where's the cinnamon?

20
00:01:20,710 --> 00:01:20,730
If there is any cinnamon,

21
00:01:20,730 --> 00:01:33,470
it's in the cabinet with the salt and pepper.

22
00:01:33,470 --> 00:01:39,860
Salt, pepper, dill weed, garlic powder, cinnamon. Ellen?

23
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:41,370
Yes, Philip.

24
00:01:41,370 --> 00:01:46,040
Is it possible that we forgot to buy cinnamon?

25
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:51,640
Yes, it is possible that we forgot to buy cinnamon.

26
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:55,480
Well, how can I make my famous apple pie without cinnamon?

27
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:56,900
Good morning.

28
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:58,590
Oh, hi, Robbie. Good morning.

29
00:01:58,590 --> 00:02:01,060
Good morning. Robbie.

30
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,320
Can you do me a favor?

31
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:04,170
Sure, Dad. What?

32
00:02:04,170 --> 00:02:07,680
Remember my apple pie on Thanksgiving?

33
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:11,860
What do you love about it?

34
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:12,900
The apples?

35
00:02:12,900 --> 00:02:15,080
No. The sssss...

36
00:02:15,080 --> 00:02:16,430
Cinnamon.

37
00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:20,830
Right. We don't have any cinnamon.

38
00:02:20,830 --> 00:02:23,750
I'll go down to Henry's grocery. He's always open.

39
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:24,730
I'll get some for you.

40
00:02:24,730 --> 00:02:27,630
That's my boy!

41
00:02:27,630 --> 00:02:29,640
Oh, put your heavy jacket on, Robbie.

42
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:34,100
It's cold outside.

43
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:36,530
Alexandra might call.

44
00:02:36,530 --> 00:02:38,050
Tell her I'll call her right back.

45
00:02:38,050 --> 00:02:39,750
OK.

46
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:44,910
Thanks, Son.

47
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:59,950
Uh, why does he always have to slam the door?

48
00:02:59,950 --> 00:03:05,350
Hello.... Hello, Alexandra. How are you? ... Fine.

49
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:07,100
Robbie just went to the store.

50
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:08,370
He'll be back soon.

51
00:03:08,370 --> 00:03:10,200
He said he'll call you.

52
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:15,910
... Oh, oh, I see.... Oh ... certainly. ...

53
00:03:15,910 --> 00:03:18,710
Well, do you have the phone number there?

54
00:03:18,710 --> 00:03:24,550
... Oh ... I see.... Please, I know he wants to talk to you.... ...

55
00:03:24,550 --> 00:03:25,380
Thank you,

56
00:03:25,380 --> 00:03:29,240
and happy Thanksgiving to you and your family, too.

57
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:34,900
Try to come by later for dessert.... Bye.

58
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,380
That was Alexandra.

59
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:37,870
She and the Molinas

60
00:03:37,870 --> 00:03:40,250
are going to spend Thanksgiving with their cousins.

61
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:42,050
She doesn't have the phone number.

62
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:44,690
Oh, Robbie will be disappointed.

63
00:03:44,690 --> 00:03:46,910
He'll be grouchy.

64
00:03:46,910 --> 00:03:51,800
Maybe she'll call back. She promised.

65
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:59,520
Here's your cinnamon, Pop.

66
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:05,240
It was a dollar and sixty cents.

67
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:08,490
You forgot to ask me for the change.

68
00:04:08,490 --> 00:04:18,110
Or did you forget to give it to me?

69
00:04:18,110 --> 00:04:21,450
Thanks, Son.

70
00:04:21,450 --> 00:04:23,270
Alexandra called.

71
00:04:23,270 --> 00:04:24,410
I'll call her back.

72
00:04:24,410 --> 00:04:26,060
She said she'll call you later.

73
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:38,030
She's not at home.

74
00:04:38,030 --> 00:04:39,720
You should have your breakfast, Son.

75
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,490
Make you feel better.

76
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:43,230
Protein, vitamins.

77
00:04:43,230 --> 00:04:44,950
She said she'll call back?

78
00:04:44,950 --> 00:04:47,740
Yes, she did.

79
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:49,300
Good morning, everyone!

80
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:52,610
Happy Turkey Day!

81
00:04:52,610 --> 00:04:53,810
What's wrong?

82
00:04:53,810 --> 00:04:59,040
Nothing. Absolutely nothing.

83
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:01,140
What's gotten into him?

84
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:03,210
He missed a phone call.

85
00:05:03,210 --> 00:05:04,210
From ...?

86
00:05:04,210 --> 00:05:08,060
Yes, Alexandra.

87
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:13,340
It's nice to see young love.... Oh, to be young again!

88
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:16,340
Where's the coffee?
